text:
Probably more, but not necessarily functionality users requested or even know about.<p>Case in point: VSCode has a multistage &quot;upgrade project to the latest .NET runtime with Copilot&quot; process that takes several minutes of processing punctuated by frequent authorization prompts for even the most trivial project, resulting in the functional equivalent of<p><pre><code>   find . -iname &#x27;*.csproj&#x27; | xargs sed -E -i.bak &#x27;s&#x2F;(&lt;TargetFramework&gt;net)8(\.0&lt;\&#x2F;TargetFramework&gt;)&#x2F;\110\2&#x2F;&#x27;
</code></pre>
along the happy path.<p>It has many more features than my shell command, of course, but none that I care about when migrating trivial projects from runtime version <i>n</i>-1 that are unlikely to hit breaking runtime or compiler changes that don&#x27;t elicit warnings from the toolchain.
